@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@ THE CONTRACT, restated from `run_backtest`'s docstring and nothing else:
     * a signal at bar t fills at the OPEN of bar t+1
     * stop and target are checked intrabar on subsequent bars, low against stop for longs and
       high against target; if both are touched in one bar the STOP is assumed first
+    * a bar after the entry bar that OPENS through the stop exits at that open, not at the stop
     * after `ttl_bars` bars without a stop or target the position closes at the next open
     * one position at a time: a signal inside a live trade is ignored
     * R = (exit - entry) * side / (entry - stop) * side, i.e. distance to stop is 1R, and the
@@ -73,6 +74,12 @@ def replay(df: pd.DataFrame, signals: Sequence[Any], cost_price_units: float = 0
         ttl = max(1, int(s.ttl_bars))
         exit_i, exit_px, reason = None, None, ""
         for j in range(entry_i, min(entry_i + ttl, len(o))):
+            # A bar AFTER the entry bar that opens through the stop fills at its open: a touched
+            # stop is a market order and the open is the first price there is (2026-11-11, the
+            # same rule as engine.run_backtest; paying the stop level there was optimistic).
+            if j > entry_i and side * (float(o[j]) - stop) <= 0:
+                exit_i, exit_px, reason = j, float(o[j]), "stop"
+                break
             if side > 0:
                 if lo[j] <= s.stop:
                     exit_i, exit_px, reason = j, float(s.stop), "stop"
